---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import { wi, order } from '../data/site.js';
import pricing from '../data/pricing.json';
import WhatsApp from '../components/WhatsApp.astro';
const g = pricing.products['google-prewarmed'];
const gf = pricing.products['google-fresh'];
const gfLow = Math.min(...gf.tiers.flatMap((t) => Object.values(t.perUnit)));
const money = (n) => (Number.isInteger(n) ? `$${n}` : `$${n.toFixed(2)}`);
const faqs = [
  ['What is the difference between prewarmed and fresh inboxes?', 'The same licensed mailbox, at two points in its life. Prewarmed arrives on a prewarmed domain that has already been aged 30 days and warmed 21, and sends on arrival. Fresh is built on your own domain and warmed for you for 14 to 21 days before it sends.'],
  ['How long until a fresh inbox can send cold email?', 'Once its warmup is done: 14 to 21 days after delivery. Every order, prewarmed or fresh, is delivered within 48 to 72 hours of payment.'],
  ['Do I need a warmup tool for fresh inboxes?', 'No. Warm Inboxes warms them for 14 to 21 days before you send, and keeps warmup running at 30 emails per inbox per day underneath your campaigns on both products.'],
  ['Is prewarmed worth the extra cost?', 'It depends on your start date. If you need to send this week, fresh cannot get there. If your launch is three weeks or more out, or you want your own brand on the domain, fresh is the better buy.'],
  ['Can I mix the two?', 'That is what most teams sending seriously end up doing. Prewarmed for the campaign that starts now, fresh on their own brand warming behind it. It is cheaper than either extreme.'],
];
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [{ '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })) }],
};
---
<Base title="Prewarmed vs Fresh Inboxes: Which to Buy, and When"
      description="The same mailbox sold at two points in its life. What the price gap actually buys, when fresh is the better purchase, and the arithmetic that decides it."
      schema={schema}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> <span class="muted">›</span> <span class="muted">Prewarmed vs fresh</span></p>
      <p class="eyebrow">Compare</p>
      <h1>Prewarmed vs fresh inboxes</h1>
      <p class="lede">The same mailbox at two points in its life. Prewarmed sends on arrival; fresh is built on your own domain and warmed for you first. Which to buy is about your start date, not the price.</p>
      <p class="cta"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/calculator/">Put your dates in →</a></p>

      <div class="scroll-x">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th></th><th>Prewarmed</th><th>Fresh</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Delivered</td><td>Within 48 to 72 hours</td><td>Within 48 to 72 hours</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ready to send</td><td class="yes">On arrival</td><td>After 14 to 21 days of warmup</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Domain</td><td class="yes">Prewarmed .com or .co, aged 30 days +</td><td class="yes">Your own brand</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Domain cost</td><td class="yes">Free</td><td>Bring your own free, or ${pricing.products['domain-fresh'].price} one off</td></tr>
            <tr><td>SPF, DKIM, DMARC and MX</td><td class="yes">Set before handover</td><td class="yes">Set before handover</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Warming tool</td><td class="yes">None needed</td><td class="yes">None needed, warmup included</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Google, per inbox per month</td><td>{money(g.perUnit.monthly)} to {money(g.perUnit.quarterly)}</td><td class="yes">{money(gf.fromPrice)} to {money(gfLow)}, by size and cycle</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>The comparison people get wrong</h2>
      <p>Put the two per-inbox prices side by side and fresh wins easily, about a third of the prewarmed price at volume. That comparison treats them as the same product at different prices, and they are not. Prewarmed is a mailbox plus a domain that has already done its weeks, sending the day it lands. Fresh is a mailbox on your own domain that sends three weeks later.</p>
      <p>Both arrive within 48 to 72 hours with SPF, DKIM and DMARC set, and both are warmed by Warm Inboxes, so neither needs a warmup tool. The real difference is the calendar, and what three weeks of not sending costs your business.</p>

      <h2>When fresh is the right call</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your first send is three weeks or more away, so the warmup fits inside time you already had.</li>
        <li>You want your own brand on the sending domain. Prewarmed inboxes stay on their prewarmed domain.</li>
        <li>You are adding capacity behind a fleet that is already sending, at the lower price per inbox.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>And if you are somewhere in between, split it: buy prewarmed for what is live now and let a fresh batch on your own brand warm behind it.</p>

      <h2>When prewarmed is the right call</h2>
      <p>A client campaign that starts next week. A domain you have just retired and need capacity to replace this week. A launch date that is fixed and close. In each of those the cheaper line item is the more expensive decision, and the gap is not the price difference. It is the weeks of meetings you do not get.</p>

      <h2>Work out which you are</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/calculator/">calculator</a> takes your daily send target and your launch date, sizes the infrastructure on each of the three platforms, prices both ways, and tells you whether fresh can reach your date at all.</p>

      <h2>The pages for each</h2>
      <p><strong>Prewarmed:</strong> <a href="/prewarmed-google-inboxes/">Google Workspace</a>, <a href="/prewarmed-microsoft-365-inboxes/">Microsoft 365</a>, <a href="/prewarmed-azure-inboxes/">Azure tenants</a>, <a href="/prewarmed-domains/">domains</a>.</p>
      <p><strong>Fresh:</strong> <a href="/fresh-google-inboxes/">Google Workspace</a>, <a href="/fresh-microsoft-365-inboxes/">Microsoft 365</a>, <a href="/fresh-azure-inboxes/">Azure tenants</a>, <a href="/fresh-domains/">domains</a>.</p>

      <Faq faqs={faqs} />

      <p class="cta end"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={order({ page: 'prewarmed-vs-fresh', placement: 'footer-cta' })} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get inboxes at Warm Inboxes</a> <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/calculator/">Run the numbers →</a> <WhatsApp /></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 780px; }
  .crumb { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-2); margin: 0 0 26px; }
  h1 { margin: 12px 0 18px; }
  h2 { margin: 50px 0 16px; }
  p { color: var(--text-2); }
  p strong { color: var(--text); }
  li { color: var(--text-2); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; }
  .cta { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 28px 0 34px; }
  .cta.end { margin-top: 44px; }
</style>
